- Charity receipt for Habitat for Humanity ($800)
- Documentation for the home office: floor plan, proof of exclusive use, rent statements, utility bills (if you plan to allocate utilities), and proof of square footage
- Receipts/invoices for the $650 business expenses (if those are business expenses)

10) Other practical notes / recommendations
- Double‑check whether the $650 expenses are business vs employee expenses — if business, include on Schedule C; if employee, not deductible.
- Use the actual home‑office method if you can document rent + utilities because your rent allocation ($3,200) is substantially larger than the simplified $650.
