Details and calculations

1) Income to report
- W-2 wages: $91,000 — reported on Form 1040 using the W-2.
- Self-employment (contracting): $15,000 — report on Schedule C (Profit or Loss from Business). Deduct business expenses on Schedule C (home office portion if applicable, contractor expenses, supplies, mileage if applicable).
- Interest from Marcus: $1,780 and from Interactive Brokers: $480 — report as interest or dividend income. Total interest/ordinary dividends = $2,260 (> $1,500) so you must file Schedule B (Interest and Ordinary Dividends).
