What you can and cannot deduct (federal)
- Self‑employment business expenses:
  - Your contracting income (15k) is reported on Schedule C. Business expenses that are ordinary and necessary for that work are deductible on Schedule C (examples: supplies, software, mileage, phone portion, home office). If the $650 “unreimbursed expenses” are business-related for the contracting work, include them on Schedule C. If they are unreimbursed employee expenses for your W‑2 employer, they generally are NOT deductible (suspended through 2025).
