  - Include the $480 from Interactive Brokers on your return as reported on your 1099 (interest, dividends, or capital gains as appropriate). Keep brokerage 1099s.

Do I itemize or take the standard deduction?
- For 2024 the standard deduction (married filing jointly) is $29,200. (If you have other itemizable items—mortgage interest, substantial state/local taxes up to $10k SALT cap, large charitable gifts, high medical expenses above AGI thresholds—they could push you to itemize.)
