What you can (generally) deduct
- Self‑employment business expenses (Schedule C)
  - You must report the $15k contracting as business income on Schedule C.
  - Ordinary and necessary business expenses are deductible on Schedule C (software, supplies, contractor expenses, business mileage, phone portion, etc.). If the $650 unreimbursed expenses relate to the contracting work, they belong on Schedule C and are deductible. If they were unreimbursed expenses for your W‑2 employer, they are not deductible for federal tax (suspended since 2018).
